Load the navmesh on a new map even after a map without one.

When a map has no navmesh, loadNavigationData() sets the status to
NAVMESH_STATUS_FAILED, and AIMGR_IsBotEnabled() is false while it is.
AIMGR_NewMap() returned early on that same check, before the unload that
resets the status to pending, so the failure carried over: after one map
without a navmesh, bots never joined again until mp_botsenabled was
toggled or the server restarted. Check the cvar instead, and always
unload (it frees only what is loaded).

--- a/main/source/mod/AvHAIPlayerManager.cpp
+++ b/main/source/mod/AvHAIPlayerManager.cpp
@@ -1018,12 +1018,14 @@
 {
 	AIMGR_BotPrecache();
 
-	if (!AIMGR_IsBotEnabled()) { return; } // Do nothing if we're not using bots. Data will be already cleared if bot is disabled via AIMGR_OnBotDisabled()
+	// Not AIMGR_IsBotEnabled(): it is also false while the navmesh status is
+	// NAVMESH_STATUS_FAILED, so one map without a navmesh would keep the bots
+	// off on every later map.
+	if (avh_botsenabled.value <= 0) { return; } // Do nothing if we're not using bots. Data will be already cleared if bot is disabled via AIMGR_OnBotDisabled()
 
-	if (NavmeshLoaded())
-	{
-		UnloadNavigationData();
-	}
+	// Unconditionally: this also resets the navmesh status to pending, so the
+	// new map's navmesh is loaded even after a failed load on the previous map
+	UnloadNavigationData();
 
 	AITAC_ClearMapAIData(true);
 
